Reading from streams
As I said, reading is a one-way operation. Whatever your current index, you will always
read from the stream one byte at a time, and in doing so, move your cursor forward by one
in the index. So, your next Read operation always starts one byte after wherever you last
read. The trick here is that every time you want to read anything more than a single byte
(which you can simply assign to a variable of the byte type), you have to read it into a
destination array. So, you'll need to declare and assign a target destination array before you
